:: Temple Companion Duties Widgets [widget]
<<widget 'temple-companion-check'>>
  <<temple-duty-check>>
  <<set _companionName to _args[0]>>
  <<temple-companion-time _companionName `_args[1] ?? 0`>>
  <<set _companionFree to _dutyToday and $temple_rank is 'priest' and _templeCompanionTime>>
  <<if _companionName is 'Robin'>>
    <<set _companionFree to _companionFree and maplebirch.get('RobinTemple')?.rank is 'priest'
      and maplebirch.get('RobinTemple').available and getRobinLocation() is 'temple'
      and !$RobinTemple.punish and $RobinTemple.monthly_checked
      and $RobinTemple.chastity_timer gt 0 and C.npc.Robin.virginity.temple is true>>
    <<if (_args[1] ?? 0) gt 0>>
      <<robin-temple-prayer-time _args[1]>>
      <<set _companionFree to _companionFree and _robinPrayerTime>>
    <</if>>
  <<elseif _companionName is 'Sydney'>>
    <<sydneySchedule>>
    <<set _companionFree to _companionFree and $sydney?.rank is 'priest'
      and C.npc.Sydney.init is 1 and C.npc.Sydney.state is 'active'
      and _sydney_location is 'temple' and $sydney_templeWork isnot 'mass'
      and $daily.sydney.punish isnot 1 and C.npc.Sydney.virginity.temple is true>>
  <<else>>
    <<set _companionFree to false>>
  <</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget 'temple-companion-shift'>>
  <<set _shiftName to $TempleDuties.speaker>>
  <<set _shiftUsed to false>>
  <<capture _shiftName _shiftUsed>>
    <<socialiseicon>>
    <<lanLink _args[0]>>
      <<temple-companion-check _shiftName 30>>
      <<if !_shiftUsed and _companionFree>>
        <<set _shiftUsed to true>>
        <<set _shiftSource to $passage>>
        <<pass 30>>
        <<temple-companion-check _shiftName 0>>
        <<if $passage is _shiftSource and !$nextPassageCheck and _companionFree>>
          <<set $TempleDuties.duty_day to Math.floor(Time.days)>>
          <<set $TempleDuties.duties += 1>>
          <<set $TempleDuties.speaker to _shiftName>>
          <<set $TempleDuties.note to 'joint-' + _shiftName>>
          <<if _shiftName is 'Robin'>>
            <<housekeeping 2>>
            <<set maplebirch.get('RobinTemple').faith += 1>>
            <<money 3000 'templeDuty'>>
          <<else>>
            <<historyskill 1>>
            <<mathsskill 1>>
            <<money 3500 'templeDuty'>>
          <</if>>
          <<grace 1>>
          <<stress -2>>
          <<npcincr _shiftName love 1>>
          <<goto 'Revelation Temple Companion Shift'>>
        <</if>>
      <</if>>
    <</lanLink>>
  <</capture>>
<</widget>>

:: Revelation Temple Sealed Note
<<temple-duty-place>>
<<if !_dutyOffice or !_bishopKnown or !$TempleDuties.enrolled
    or ['refused', 'reported'].includes($TempleDuties.bishop)>>
  <<temple-duty-back>>
  <<exit>>
<</if>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    You recognise the dark wax seal. The note asks you to compare the returned crate's mark with the old relief records. It gives no name for the sender. "A copy for our hands, child. Keep the public account accurate."
    A smaller sheet is tucked inside: "Leave your answer with the clerk."
  <<option 'CN'>>
    你认出那枚深色蜡封。便条请你把退回货箱上的标记与旧救济记录比对，没有写寄件人的姓名。“给我们的双手留一份副本，孩子。公开账目仍要如实填写。”
    里面夹着一张小纸：“答复留给侍从。”
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<if $TempleDuties.bishop isnot 'accepted'>>
  <<socialiseicon>>
  <<temple-duty-action `['Agree to compare the records (0:05)', '答应核对记录 (0:05)']` 5 'Revelation Temple Sealed Answer'>>
    <<set $TempleDuties.bishop to 'accepted'>>
    <<set $TempleDuties.note to 'bishop-accepted'>>
  <</temple-duty-action>>
  <br>
  <<refuseicon>>
  <<temple-duty-action `['Decline the private request (0:05)', '拒绝这份私下委托 (0:05)']` 5 'Revelation Temple Sealed Answer'>>
    <<set $TempleDuties.bishop to 'refused'>>
    <<set $TempleDuties.note to 'bishop-refused'>>
  <</temple-duty-action>>
  <br>
<<elseif !$TempleDuties.bishop_checked>>
  <span class='lblue'><<lanSwitch 'You need the delivery records, a truthful report on the returned crate, and a comparison made in the old records room.' '需要旧交货记录、如实填写的货箱调查报告，再到旧资料室完成比对。'>></span><br>
  <<icon 'temple/records-room.png'>>
  <<lanLink ['Go to the records room', '前往资料室'] 'Temple Library'>>
  <</lanLink>>
  <br>
<<elseif $per_npc.bishop>>
  <<socialiseicon 'ask'>>
  <<temple-duty-action `['Take the sealed copy to the waiting confessor (0:05)', '把密封副本交给等候的告解员 (0:05)']` 5 'Revelation Temple Bishop'>>
    <<if $TempleDuties.bishop is 'accepted' and $TempleDuties.bishop_checked>>
      <<set $TempleDuties.bishop to 'reported'>>
      <<historyskill 3>>
    <</if>>
  <</temple-duty-action>>
  <br>
<<else>>
  <span class='lblue'><<lanSwitch 'No confessor is waiting. Keep the sealed copy until your original contact can receive it.' '没有告解员在等候。保存副本，等原先的联络人能够接收。'>></span><br>
<</if>>
<br>
<<temple-duty-back>>

:: Revelation Temple Sealed Answer
<<temple-duty-place>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    <<switch $TempleDuties.note>>
      <<case 'bishop-accepted'>>
        You leave a brief acceptance in the folded note. The original reports remain in the duties book; only the comparison will be copied.
      <<case 'bishop-refused'>>
        You write that you will keep to your public duties. The messenger takes the folded note without arguing. Jordan's duties book remains where you left it.
      <<case 'bishop-checked'>>
        The old ledger gives a weight and a collection date, but no matching signature. You copy those omissions as well as the mark. They may matter to the confessors; they do not prove who sent the crate.
    <</switch>>
  <<option 'CN'>>
    <<switch $TempleDuties.note>>
      <<case 'bishop-accepted'>>
        你在折好的便条里留下简短答复。原始报告仍留在职务簿里，只会抄出比对结果。
      <<case 'bishop-refused'>>
        你写明只承担公开职务。传话者没有争辩，接过折好的便条。约旦的职务簿仍在原处。
      <<case 'bishop-checked'>>
        旧账簿写着重量和提货日期，却没有对应的签字。你把缺失的部分与标记一并抄下。这些也许对告解员有用，却不能证明是谁寄了货箱。
    <</switch>>
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<temple-duty-back>>

:: Revelation Temple Bishop
<<temple-duty-place>>
<<if $TempleDuties.bishop isnot 'reported' or !$per_npc.bishop>>
  <<temple-duty-back>>
  <<exit>>
<</if>>
<<loadNPC 0 'bishop'>>
<<person1>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    The messenger guides you through a side door. The bishop breaks the seal, smiling over the page. "You even copied what was missing. Most people prefer to fill the empty space."
    <<He>> folds the comparison into <<his>> robe. "Jordan's people need a safe room and an honest ledger. We may need to find who left it otherwise." <<He>> lets the last word hang. "You've promised a report, child. Nothing more."
    The messenger opens the side door for you. You fold your copy of the ledger into your pocket.
  <<option 'CN'>>
    传话者领你穿过侧门。主教拆开封印，低头读着，露出笑容。“你连缺失的部分也抄了。多数人更喜欢把空白填满。”
    <<He>>把比对结果折进袍里。“约旦的人需要安全的房间与真实的账簿。我们也许需要找到让它变得不安全的人。”<<He>>让这句话停了一会儿。“你答应的是报告，孩子。仅此而已。”
    传话者替你打开侧门。你把账簿的副本折好，收进口袋。
<</language>>
<br><br>
<<temple-manor-offer>>
<br>
<<getouticon>>
<<lanLink ['Return through the side door', '从侧门返回'] 'Revelation Temple Office'>>
  <<endevent>>
<</lanLink>>
<br>

:: Revelation Temple Companion
<<temple-duty-place>>
<<if !_dutySafe or !$TempleDuties.speaker
    or ($TempleDuties.speaker is 'Robin' and getRobinLocation() isnot 'temple')
    or ($TempleDuties.speaker is 'Sydney' and (_sydney_location isnot 'temple' or $daily.sydney.punish is 1))>>
  <<lanSwitch 'The person you meant to speak to has another duty now. You can talk when you next meet here.' '你想交谈的人已经有了别的安排。下次在这里遇见时，可以再聊。'>><br><br>
  <<temple-duty-back>>
  <<exit>>
<</if>>
<<npc `$TempleDuties.speaker`>>
<<person1>>
<<if $TempleDuties.speaker is 'Robin'>>
  <<language>>
    <<option 'EN'>>
      Robin rests a bundle of blankets against the pew.
      <<if C.npc.Robin.trauma gte 40>>
        "Please don't stay down there if it feels wrong," <<he>> says. "Even if they expect you to."
      <<elseif C.npc.Robin.dom gte 50>>
        "Check your lamp before you go," <<he>> says, tugging the rope loose to look at its end. "And come back with a story I can understand."
      <<else>>
        "I can check the list with you," <<he>> offers. "I'm no good at the other part, but I can count."
      <</if>>
      <<if maplebirch.get('RobinTemple').rank is 'priest'>>
        Robin opens the prayer book at a folded corner. "Someone asked for me today," <<he>> says. "I kept looking behind me for Jordan." <<He>> glances at the lower door. "Then I remembered where you stood."
      <<elseif $temple_rank is 'priest'>>
        "A priest," Robin repeats, smiling uncertainly. "Does that mean you'll be even busier?" You explain the shifts are still yours to accept. <<He>> looks relieved.
      <</if>>
    <<option 'CN'>>
      罗宾把一捆毯子靠在长椅边。
      <<if C.npc.Robin.trauma gte 40>>
        “感觉不对就别留在下面，”<<he>>说，“就算他们希望你留下也一样。”
      <<elseif C.npc.Robin.dom gte 50>>
        “出发前检查灯，”<<he>>说，把绳子松开，查看末端。“回来时，讲个我能听明白的经过。”
      <<else>>
        “我可以和你核对清单，”<<he>>提议，“另一部分我不擅长，但数数总可以。”
      <</if>>
      <<if maplebirch.get('RobinTemple').rank is 'priest'>>
        罗宾翻到祷书折角的那一页。“今天有人找我，”<<he>>说，“我一直回头，想找约旦。”<<He>>望向下层的门。“后来，我想起了你站过的地方。”
      <<elseif $temple_rank is 'priest'>>
        “司祭啊。”罗宾重复了一遍，带着些不确定的笑。“你以后会更忙吗？”你解释，是否接班仍由自己决定。<<He>>松了口气。
      <</if>>
  <</language>>
<<else>>
  <<run statusCheck('Sydney')>>
  <<language>>
    <<option 'EN'>>
      Sydney puts a bookmark between the pages.
      <<if _sydneyStatus.includes('pure')>>
        "Jordan always checks the names first," <<he>> says. "I used to think that was just the paperwork. It isn't, is it?"
      <<else>>
        "People like a brave story," <<he>> says, lowering <<his>> voice. "It doesn't have to be what you put in the report." <<He>> smiles, then checks the list seriously.
      <</if>>
      <<if $sydney.rank is 'priest'>>
        Sydney sets a small key beside the bookmark. "Jordan gave me this after the prayers. I know which door it fits." <<He>> pauses, listening to something beyond the wall. "I'll wait until <<nnpc_he 'Jordan'>> comes with me."
      <<elseif $temple_rank is 'priest'>>
        "Congratulations," <<he>> says. "I'll try not to make you start by correcting my handwriting." <<He>> straightens the books.
      <</if>>
    <<option 'CN'>>
      悉尼把书签夹进页间。
      <<if _sydneyStatus.includes('pure')>>
        “约旦总先核对名字，”<<he>>说，“以前我以为只是文书工作。其实不是，对吧？”
      <<else>>
        “大家都爱听英勇的故事，”<<he>>压低声音，“但报告不必那样写。”<<He>>笑了笑，又认真核对清单。
      <</if>>
      <<if $sydney.rank is 'priest'>>
        悉尼在书签旁放下一把小钥匙。“祈祷后，约旦把它交给我。我知道它能开哪扇门。”<<He>>停了一会儿，像是在听墙后的动静。“等<<nnpc_he 'Jordan'>>陪我去。”
      <<elseif $temple_rank is 'priest'>>
        “恭喜，”<<he>>说，“我会尽量不让你上任第一件事就是纠正我的字。”<<He>>把书摆正。
      <</if>>
  <</language>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<temple-companion-check $TempleDuties.speaker 30>>
<<if _companionFree>>
  <<if $TempleDuties.speaker is 'Robin'>>
    <<temple-companion-shift `['Take the blanket handover with Robin (£30 0:30)', '和罗宾接一班毯子交接 (£30 0:30)']`>>
    <<ghousekeeping>>
    <<ggrace>>
    <<glove 'Robin'>>
    <<lstress>><br>
  <<else>>
    <<temple-companion-shift `['Check the archive receipts with Sydney (£35 0:30)', '和悉尼核对档案收据 (£35 0:30)']`>>
    <<ghistory>>
    <<gmaths>>
    <<ggrace>>
    <<glove 'Sydney'>>
    <<lstress>><br>
  <</if>>
<</if>>
<<temple-duty-back>>

:: Revelation Temple Companion Shift
<<temple-duty-place>>
<<if $TempleDuties.duty_day isnot Math.floor(Time.days)
    or !['joint-Robin', 'joint-Sydney'].includes($TempleDuties.note)>>
  <<temple-duty-back>>
  <<exit>>
<</if>>
<<npc `$TempleDuties.speaker`>>
<<person1>>
<<if $TempleDuties.speaker is 'Sydney'>>
  <<run statusCheck('Sydney')>>
<</if>>
<<language>>
  <<option 'EN'>>
    <<if $TempleDuties.speaker is 'Robin'>>
      Robin unfolds the list before handing over the blankets. A visitor cannot remember the name on the request. <<if C.npc.Robin.trauma gte 40>><<He>> hesitates, then pulls a chair nearer. "You can sit while we find it."<<elseif C.npc.Robin.dom gte 50>>"One thing at a time," <<he>> says. "Tell us where you stayed last night."<<else>><<He>> checks the next name with you quietly before asking the visitor again.<</if>> You count the dry bundles while <<he>> listens. The missing name turns up on the back of the page. "I would have rushed past that," Robin admits. <<He>> checks the clock before you both leave the signed handover. Jordan has set your pay beside it.
    <<else>>
      Sydney sets the old receipt beside the new entry and asks you to read the names back. <<if _sydneyStatus.includes('pure')>><<He>> apologises when a page sticks, then smooths it carefully before continuing. "They should be able to find their own name."<<else>>"A heroic account, three spelling mistakes," <<he>> murmurs. The smile fades when <<he>> finds the wrong collection date. "That part needs fixing."<</if>> You follow the ink through the copied pages, checking the sums together. Sydney puts the key away and glances towards the hall before the next duty. Jordan signs the corrected receipt and leaves your pay with the clerk.
    <</if>>
  <<option 'CN'>>
    <<if $TempleDuties.speaker is 'Robin'>>
      交出毯子前，罗宾先展开名单。一名访客想不起申请时写下的名字。<<if C.npc.Robin.trauma gte 40>><<He>>迟疑了一下，把椅子拉近。“找的时候，你可以先坐着。”<<elseif C.npc.Robin.dom gte 50>>“一件件来，”<<he>>说，“先告诉我们，昨晚住在哪里。”<<else>><<He>>低声与你核对下一个名字，再问访客一遍。<</if>>你清点干毯子，<<he>>听对方说。漏掉的名字就在纸背面。“我可能会急着翻过去。”罗宾承认。留下签好的交接记录前，<<he>>看了一眼钟。约旦已经把你的报酬放在旁边。
    <<else>>
      悉尼把旧收据放在新记录旁，请你读回名字。<<if _sydneyStatus.includes('pure')>>一页纸粘住了，<<he>>先道歉，再仔细展平。“他们也该找得到自己的名字。”<<else>>“一份英勇的记录，三个错字。”<<he>>低声说。发现收货日期不对时，笑容便收起来了。“这里得改。”<</if>>你沿着几页抄录的笔迹查下去，与<<him>>一起核对金额。悉尼收好钥匙，在下项事务前望了望大厅。约旦在更正的收据上签字，把你的报酬交给侍从。
    <</if>>
<</language>>
<<ggrace>>
<<lstress>>
<<glove `$TempleDuties.speaker`>>
<br><br>
<<temple-duty-rest-link>>
<<temple-duty-back>>
